# uncertainty-must-surface-not-pass-through

Any form of uncertainty encountered at a planning pipeline stage — incomplete data, contradictory entries, unverified estimates, or ambiguity — must be surfaced as an explicit halt or named alert and never absorbed, glossed over, or forwarded downstream. Downstream consumers must receive only complete, verified, non-contradictory inputs.

## Procedures
- At each pipeline stage, validate inputs for completeness, consistency, and absence of estimates before processing.
- If validation fails, emit a named alert (e.g. PLAN_INCONSISTENCY_ALERT) and halt — do not produce partial output.
- Never substitute estimates, defaults, or preliminary figures for confirmed values; block the stage instead.
- Document the specific gap or contradiction so the upstream source can correct it before re-entry.

